===Etymology===
From {{etyl|VL.|it}} *''raglāre'' < *{{term||ragulāre}}, from {{etyl|LL.|it}} {{m|la|ragere}} (whence French {{m|fr|raire}}, {{m|fr|réer}}, Romanian {{m|ro|rage}}). Compare Venetian {{m|vec|rajar}}, {{m|vec|ragiar}}, Sicilian {{m|scn|ragghiari}}, French {{m|fr|railler}}, Occitan {{m|oc|ralhar}}, Catalan {{m|ca|rallar}}. The form {{m|it|ragliare}} in Italian may have been influenced by a northern Italian variant or Gallo-Romance language (cf. Old Provençal {{m|pro|ralhar}}); compare the original form {{m|it|ragghiare}}.

